1. Introduction

1.1 Motivation

Human conversation is not an input–output transformation. A listener infers beliefs, intentions, sincerity, likely next utterances, and the social consequences of possible responses. Much of this processing occurs without observable output. The absence of behavior does not imply the absence of internal dynamics.

Contemporary LLMs perform substantial latent computation (Quiet-STaR [1]; Coconut [2]; pause tokens [3]; Huginn [4]). However, the architecturally relevant distinction is not human thought vs. token prediction, but:

\textbf{reactive computation} \quad\text{vs.}\quad \textbf{persistent recurrent interactive dynamics}.

1.2 Two orthogonal axes: depth and persistence

Existing literature conflates two independent properties:

· Depth axis d: number of internal refinement steps K per external observation (Coconut, looped transformers, Huginn).
· Persistence axis \tau: horizon over which the recurrent state R_t is preserved (Transformer-XL [5]; Compressive Transformer [6]; Mamba [7]; RMT [8]).

Coconut achieves d > 1 but \tau = 0 across turns. Huginn achieves d \gg 1 and \tau = \text{sequence-length} but resets between tasks. Transformer-XL and Mamba achieve \tau > 1 but d = 1. HIL claims (d > 1, \tau \geq 10) with explicit Self/Other factorization.

1.3 Contribution of v0.3

· Formal separation of depth and persistence (§3.1).
· Refined identification of O_t via causal abstraction + DAS + path patching, replacing post-hoc SAE clamping (§4).
· Time-unrolled structural causal model (SCM) with path-specific effects (§5).
· Explicitly matched-compute four-architecture experiment (§6).
· Task redesign: removal of saturated Sally-Anne; adoption of FANToM-extended, NegotiationToM, LIFELONG-SOTOPA (§7).
· Pre-registered quantitative falsification criteria (§11).
· Architectural factorization as a training objective rather than a post-hoc interpretability claim (§4.4).

