3. Formal Framework

3.1 State space

For a minimal proof of concept, four variables:

X_t = (W_t, S_t, O_t, R_t) \in \mathbb{R}^{d_W} \times \mathbb{R}^{d_S} \times \mathbb{R}^{d_O} \times \mathbb{R}^{d_R}

Symbol Meaning
W_t World model (task, environment)
S_t Self model (goals, beliefs, intentions)
O_t Other-agent model (distribution over interlocutor hidden state Y_B)
R_t Re-entry / recurrent carrier state

The full eight-variable decomposition (W, S, O, P, C, M, E, R) remains conceptual and is deferred to future work.

3.2 Depth and persistence

Define:

d := K \quad\text{(internal steps per observation)}, \qquad \tau := \text{(turns over which } R_t \text{ is preserved)}.

HIL targets (d = 4\text{–}8,\ \tau \geq 10).

3.3 Internal dynamics

Given observation u_t (a user turn), the system initializes:

X_{t,0} = G(u_t, X_{t-1,K})

and performs K internal transitions:

X_{t,k+1} = F(X_{t,k}, u_t, \epsilon_{t,k}), \quad k = 0, \dots, K-1.

The final action is a_t = \pi(X_{t,K}).

Crucially, X_{t,k+1} \neq X_{t,k} even when no external token is emitted. This separates external time t from internal computational time k.

3.4 Gated recurrent update (normalized)

Replacing the v0.2 update with a LayerNorm + GRU-forget-gate formulation:

X'_{t,k} = \mathrm{LN}\!\left( X_{t,k} + \alpha \cdot \mathrm{Attn}\!\left(Q = X_{t,k},\ K = [u_t; R_{t,k}],\ V = [u_t; R_{t,k}]\right) \right),

R_{t,k+1} = \mathrm{GRU}\!\left(R_{t,k},\ X'_{t,k}\right),

with learnable gate \alpha \in (0,1). This is Transformer-XL + RMT with explicit compression at the R_t bottleneck.

3.5 Re-entry (time-unrolled)

Re-entry is a two-phase read-back, defined at each internal step:

X'_{t,k} = F(X_{t,k}, u_t), \qquad R_{t,k} = F_R(X'_{t,k}), \qquad X_{t,k+1} = G(X'_{t,k}, R_{t,k}).

This avoids circular self-reference while preserving the idea that the result of one internal computation feeds the next. The SCM (§5) is defined on the unrolled graph, not on the cyclic macro-graph.

