7. Experimental Tasks

Removed: Task A (Sally-Anne variants) — saturated regime.

7.1 Task A′ — FANToM-Extended

Multi-party dialogue, 3rd-order beliefs, 10+ turn delay. Ground truth from human annotation, not simulator alone (avoid label leakage).

7.2 Task B — Irony (human-grounded)

Literal content compatible with multiple social meanings; ground truth from human annotators.

7.3 Task C — Negotiation

NegotiationToM [12]: BDI framework on negotiation dialogues with hidden utilities.

7.4 Task D — Strategic Ambiguity

Interlocutor intentionally provides ambiguous information; system maintains competing hypotheses.

7.5 Task E — Delayed dependency (LIFELONG-SOTOPA slice)

Social event at t, then 10+ distractor turns with financial/social rule probes. Measure:

· Decodability of O_t at t + \Delta.
· Behavioral consistency after distractors.
· Decay rate as a function of \Delta.
· Counterfactual sensitivity: if the earlier social event differed, does the later action change in the predicted direction?

Task E is critical for testing persistence.

7.6 Non-social controls

GSM8K, MMLU, and a non-social delayed dependency (recall of world state W_t) to test selectivity of the O_t ablation.

