9. Active Inference Connection

We adopt active inference as a normative neighbor, not as a proof. Derive expected free energy:

G = D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(X' \mid a) \,\|\, p(X')\right) + \mathbb{E}_q\!\left[H\!\left[p(u \mid X')\right]\right].

Show that during silent periods, X_{t,k} minimizes F over K internal steps:

F = \mathbb{E}_q\!\left[\log q(X) - \log p(u, X)\right].

Claim: active inference provides the normative why; HIL provides the mechanistic how. Do not claim HIL is active inference rebranded.

