Appendix B: Architectural Equations

B.1 HIL State Initialization

X_{t,0} = G(u_t, X_{t-1,K})

where G is a learned initialization function (MLP with residual connection).

B.2 Internal Transition (Unrolled)

For k = 0, \dots, K-1:

X_{t,k+1} = F(X_{t,k}, u_t, \epsilon_{t,k})

with stochastic noise \epsilon_{t,k} \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2 I).

B.3 Gated Recurrent Update (Normalized)

X'_{t,k} = \mathrm{LN}\!\left( X_{t,k} + \alpha \cdot \mathrm{Attn}\!\left(Q = X_{t,k},\ K = [u_t; R_{t,k}],\ V = [u_t; R_{t,k}]\right) \right)

R_{t,k+1} = \mathrm{GRU}\!\left(R_{t,k},\ X'_{t,k}\right)

with learnable gate \alpha \in (0,1), LayerNorm \mathrm{LN}, and concatenation [\cdot;\cdot] along the feature dimension.

B.4 Re-Entry (Two-Phase Read-Back)

X'_{t,k} = F(X_{t,k}, u_t)

R_{t,k} = F_R(X'_{t,k})

X_{t,k+1} = G(X'_{t,k}, R_{t,k})

This avoids circular self-reference while preserving the reentrant signaling property.

B.5 Self/Other Factorization

S_{t,k+1} = f_S\!\left(S_{t,k}, O_{t,k}, R_{t,k}, u_t\right)

O_{t,k+1} = f_O\!\left(O_{t,k}, S_{t,k}, R_{t,k}, u_t\right)

with gated cross-attention:

\alpha_{S \to O} = \sigma\!\left(W_g [S_{t,k}; O_{t,k}]\right)

O_{t,k+1} = f_O\!\left(O_{t,k} + \alpha_{S \to O} \cdot \mathrm{CrossAttn}(O_{t,k}, S_{t,k}), R_{t,k}, u_t\right)

B.6 Action Policy

a_t = \pi(X_{t,K}) = \pi(W_{t,K}, S_{t,K}, O_{t,K}, R_{t,K})

B.7 Coconut-Style Architecture (Baseline)

h_{t+1} = \mathrm{LLM}(h_t)

where h_t is the last hidden state fed back as the next input embedding. No persistent state across turns.

Reference: Hao et al., Training Large Language Models to Reason in a Continuous Latent Space (Coconut), arXiv:2412.06769.

B.8 Huginn-Style Architecture (Baseline)

h^{(r+1)} = \mathrm{Block}(h^{(r)}), \quad r = 1, \dots, R

where the same transformer block is reused R times at inference. State resets between tasks.

Reference: Geiping et al., Scaling up Test-Time Compute with Latent Reasoning: A Recurrent Depth Approach (Huginn), arXiv:2502.05171.

B.9 Mamba-Style Architecture (Baseline)

h_t = \bar{A} h_{t-1} + \bar{B} x_t

y_t = C h_t

with input-dependent \Delta, B, C. State size O(1) vs. Transformer O(L).

Reference: Gu & Dao, Mamba: Linear-Time Sequence Modeling with Selective State Spaces, arXiv:2312.00752.

B.10 RMT-Style Architecture (Baseline)

[O^t, M^t] = \mathrm{RMT}(X^t, M^{t-1})

Memory tokens M are prepended to the input sequence and passed across segments.

Reference: Bulatov et al., Recurrent Memory Transformer, arXiv:2207.06881.

B.11 Transformer-XL-Style Architecture (Baseline)

Segment-level recurrence with relative positional encoding:

h_{t+1}^{(\ell)} = \mathrm{TransformerBlock}\!\left(h_t^{(\ell-1)}, \mathrm{SG}(h_{t}^{(\ell)})\right)

where \mathrm{SG} denotes stop-gradient.

Reference: Dai et al., Transformer-XL: Attentive Language Models Beyond a Fixed-Length Context, arXiv:1901.02860.

