Appendix C: Structural Causal Model and Intervention Semantics

C.1 Unrolled SCM Definition

The macro-graph u_t \to W_t \to O_t \to P_t \to C_t \to E_t \to a_t is cyclic once re-entry is included. We define the SCM on the unrolled internal graph:

X_v^{(k+1)} = f_v\!\left(\mathrm{pa}(X_v^{(k)}), u_t, \epsilon_v^{(k)}\right), \quad k = 0, \dots, K-1

for each v \in \{W, S, O, R\}. Edges allowed per step:

Step Allowed Edges
k=0 u_t \to W, u_t \to S, u_t \to O, u_t \to R
k>0 W \to W, W \to O, S \to S, S \to O, O \to O, O \to S, R \to W, R \to S, R \to O, R \to R

C.2 Effect Definitions

Total Effect (TE):

\mathrm{TE} = \mathbb{E}[a_t \mid \mathrm{do}(O_t = \tilde{O}_t)] - \mathbb{E}[a_t \mid \mathrm{do}(O_t = O_t^*)]

Path-Specific Effect (PSE) via Path Patching:

\mathrm{TE} = \sum_{p \in \Pi(O_t \to a_t)} \mathrm{PSE}(p) + \mathrm{residual}

where \Pi is the set of directed paths in the unrolled graph.

Stochastic Policy Distributional Shift:

\Delta_a = D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi(a_t \mid \mathrm{do}(O_t = \tilde{O}_t)) \,\|\, \pi(a_t \mid \mathrm{do}(O_t = O_t^*))\right)

C.3 Path Patching Procedure

Path patching (Goldowsky-Dill et al., arXiv:2304.05969):

1. Run base input, cache all activations.
2. Run source input, cache all activations.
3. For each candidate path p:
   · Replace the activations on p in the base run with source activations.
   · Measure the change in output.
4. Rank paths by effect magnitude.

C.4 Interchange Intervention Implementation

\mathrm{do}(O_t = \tilde{O}_t) \quad\text{implemented as}\quad \mathrm{Interchange}(O_t^{\text{source}} \to O_t^{\text{base}})

This respects the causal graph and avoids off-manifold states. The interchange intervention accuracy (IIA) is the proportion of aligned interventions with equivalent high-level and low-level effects.

Reference: Geiger et al., Causal Abstraction for Interpretability, arXiv:2301.04709.

