Appendix G: Pre-Registration and Falsification Criteria

G.1 Quantitative Thresholds

Normalized Gain:

\mathrm{Gain}(M) = \frac{\mathrm{Perf}(M) - \mathrm{Perf}(\text{baseline})}{\mathrm{Perf}(\text{oracle}) - \mathrm{Perf}(\text{baseline})}

Falsification Rule: If \mathrm{Gain}(\text{HIL-no-S/O}) > 0.90 \cdot \mathrm{Gain}(\text{HIL}), H0 not rejected.

Selectivity: Social task delta > 2\times non-social task delta.

Bayesian: \mathrm{BF}_{10} > 10 required for confirmation.

G.2 Falsification Criteria

# Criterion Implication
1 HIL-no-S/O matches HIL at equal budget H1 weakened
2 Explicit O_t interventions fail Causal role unsupported
3 HIL advantage disappears after FLOP matching Compute confound
4 Standard/generic recurrent architectures reproduce persistence Architectural specificity unsupported
5 O_t contains no predictive info beyond context Redundancy
